---
/**
 * Privacy notice. DRAFT: needs JFD approval (CONTENT-TODO.md, launch blocker). Statements
 * describe how this site is actually built; controller details come from business.ts and render
 * only once confirmed. Update the analytics section if an analytics provider is added (Decision 6),
 * and the upload retention if Decision 5 changes the defaults.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/sections/Section.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business';
import { paths } from '../data/paths';
import { gaCookieless, gaId } from '../lib/analytics';

const crumbs = [{ name: 'Privacy', path: paths.privacy }];
const controller = business.legalName ?? business.name;
const office = business.registeredOffice;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice | Just Fire Doors"
  description="How Just Fire Doors SW collects, uses and protects personal information sent through this website, including enquiries and uploaded documents."
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Section tone="surface" labelledby="page-title">
    <article class="legal">
      <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} class="legal__crumbs" />
      <h1 id="page-title" class="legal__title">
        Privacy notice
      </h1>
      <p class="legal__lead">
        This notice explains how {controller} uses the personal information you give us through this
        website, and your rights over it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {controller} is the controller of the personal information described in this notice.
        {business.companyNumber && <> Company number {business.companyNumber}.</>}
        {office && (
          <>
            {' '}
            Registered office: {office.streetAddress}, {office.addressLocality}, {office.postalCode}
            .
          </>
        )}
      </p>
      <p>
        You can contact us about privacy through our <a href={paths.contact}>contact page</a>
        {business.email && (
          <>
            {' '}
            or by email at <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>
          </>
        )}
        .
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you send an enquiry or request a quote, we collect what you choose to give us:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name, organisation, email address and telephone number</li>
        <li>details about the site, the work and any deadlines</li>
        <li>
          documents and photos you upload, such as fire door surveys, inspection reports, job sheets
          and remedial schedules
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Uploaded documents can contain information about buildings and, occasionally, about people.
        Please only send what we need to understand the work.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use this information to respond to your enquiry, review the work, prepare a quotation
        and, if you instruct us, plan and deliver the work. Our lawful basis is taking steps at your
        request before entering into a contract, and our legitimate interest in responding to
        business enquiries.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it goes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Website hosting and file storage:</strong> Cloudflare hosts this website.
          Documents you upload are stored in private Cloudflare storage and are only accessible to
          our team through secure, expiring links.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email delivery:</strong> enquiry details are sent to our team by a transactional
          email service (Resend).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Spam protection:</strong> our forms use Cloudflare Turnstile, which checks that a
          person, not an automated program, is sending the form.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your information or share it for marketing.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Uploaded documents are deleted from website storage automatically after 90 days. Enquiry
        emails and any documents we save into our own records are kept for as long as needed to
        respond, deliver and support the work, and to meet our legal and accounting obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
      {gaId ? (
        <>
          {gaCookieless ? (
            <>
              <p>
                We use Google Analytics to understand how the site is used: which pages are visited,
                roughly where visitors are, and whether the forms are working.
              </p>
              <p>
                Until you make a choice in the analytics banner, this works without cookies. Each
                page view is reported to Google with a random number that is not stored on your
                device and changes on every page, so visits are counted but are not joined up into a
                browsing history. As with any web request, Google’s servers receive your IP address
                and browser details when this happens.
              </p>
              <p>
                If you accept analytics cookies, Google Analytics sets cookies (named{' '}
                <code>_ga</code> and similar) that last up to two years, which lets us see returning
                visits and how a visit unfolds. If you choose “Switch off”, nothing is sent to
                Google Analytics at all and any analytics cookies are removed.
              </p>
            </>
          ) : (
            <p>
              If you accept analytics cookies, we use Google Analytics to understand how the site is
              used: which pages are visited, roughly where visitors are, and whether the forms are
              working. Google Analytics sets cookies (named <code>_ga</code> and similar) that last
              up to two years. Nothing is loaded from Google unless you accept.
            </p>
          )}
          <p>
            Google processes this information on our behalf, which can include transferring it
            outside the UK. You can change your choice at any time with “Cookie settings” at the
            bottom of every page. We do not use advertising cookies, and we never send what you type
            into our forms to Google Analytics.
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p>
          This website does not use cookies for tracking or advertising, and does not currently use
          an analytics service.
        </p>
      )}

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to ask for a copy of your information, to have it corrected or deleted,
        to restrict or object to how we use it, and to receive it in a portable format. To use any
        of these rights, contact us using the details above.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, you can complain to the
        Information Commissioner’s Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .legal :global(.legal__crumbs) {
    margin-bottom: 26px;
  }
  .legal__title {
    font-family: var(--jfd-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 68px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.04;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .legal__lead {
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.58;
    color: var(--jfd-graphite);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-family: var(--jfd-font-display);
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--jfd-rule);
  }
  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.62;
    color: var(--jfd-ink-2);
  }
  .legal p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .legal ul {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }
  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .legal strong {
    color: var(--jfd-graphite);
  }
  .legal a {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--jfd-underline);
  }
</style>
